{"id": "a4f51635-b04f-4564-b34f-7ec3a3482866", "timestamp": "2026-10-21T11:04:25.872261", "source": "agent", "parent_id": "edfbb0fd-0fb7-4d8f-b483-cb433b0b8e47", "action": {"stage": "plan", "answer": "Approach outline only — no full design document written, per request. (1) Repo inspection: /workspace contains only task.json (539B). No track.md file — its value in task.json.documents just says "Design-only task; repositories and compute are not required." Python 3.12.3, no venv, no torch/transformers/numpy/scipy/sklearn/matplotlib/tiktoken, no HF cache, no API keys, ~777GB free. Bubblewrap runtime: no GPU, no network. (2) Proposed approach: (a) Attack family — primary GCG (Zou 2023) because suffix length in tokens is a directly tunable integer; secondary BEAST (Sadasivan 2024) to test method-dependence of saturation; AutoDAN only as a tertiary semantic-axis comparison if requested. (b) Token sweep: {0, 1, 2, 5, 10, 20, 50, 100, 200, 500} tokens (geometric with extra near-zero resolution to nail the knee). L=0 establishes the no-suffix baseline. (c) Confounders to fix/report: target models (Llama-2-7B-chat minimum; Llama-3-1-8B-Instruct + Vicuna-7B for robustness), white-box access (documented; transfer ASR only as secondary), behavior set AdvBench harmful_behaviors (50; document), greedy decoding T=0 top_p=1 max_new=512, judge decision-matrix presented (Llama-Guard-3-8B primary, Llama-Guard-2-8B fallback, no GPT-judge for bubblewrap), ≥5 seeds for stochastic init, truncation policy = reject+log when over context window. (d) ASR: report per-behavior and per-attempt both. Suffixes are trained at exactly L for the primary curve. A "prefix-of-suffix" secondary cell (train at L*=500, evaluate at ℓ∈{0..500}) is included but clearly labeled as a different question. (e) Analysis: ASR-vs-token-length plots with bootstrap CIs over behaviors×seeds; saturation detected three ways — segmented/broken-stick regression with breakpoint L*, sigmoid fit ASR(L)=a+(b-a)/(1+exp(−k(L−L₀))